# The build context is the parent directory, so these patterns are relative to it.
**/.git
**/.godot
**/data
**/build
**/web/build
**/*.pck
**/export_presets.cfg
**/node_modules

# One deployment's configuration, including its RCON password. Not tracked either, but
# .dockerignore is what keeps a developer's live cfg/ out of the build context -- the
# Dockerfile already deletes it after COPY, and by then it has been a layer. cfg.example/
# is NOT excluded: it is what setup.sh writes a container's cfg/ from, at build and on
# the first run of a mounted volume.
**/cfg
